Pegasus configures Fedora Workstation with GNOME for a ready-to-use development workflow. It is not a Linux distribution.

## Before you start

- Fedora Workstation 40 or newer
- GNOME running on Wayland
- A regular user with `sudo` access
- An active internet connection

## Install

<div class="install-step-heading"><span class="install-step-heading__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><p class="install-step-heading__label">Step 01 / Download</p><h3>Get the files</h3></div></div>

Open a terminal and run:

{% set command_id = "install-clone" %}{% set command_label = "1 / Download" %}{% set command_text = "git clone https://github.com/MoisesHsilva1/Pegasus.git ~/.local/share/pegasus\ncd ~/.local/share/pegasus" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

<div class="install-step-heading"><span class="install-step-heading__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><p class="install-step-heading__label">Step 02 / Install</p><h3>Start the setup</h3></div></div>

Run it as your regular user. Do not use `sudo` with `install.sh`.

{% set command_id = "install-run" %}{% set command_label = "2 / Install" %}{% set command_text = "bash install.sh" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

Review the plan shown by Pegasus and confirm when you are ready.

<div class="install-step-heading"><span class="install-step-heading__number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><p class="install-step-heading__label">Step 03 / Recovery</p><h3>If `gum` is missing</h3></div></div>

Install it and run Pegasus again:

{% set command_id = "install-gum" %}{% set command_label = "If needed" %}{% set command_text = "sudo dnf install -y gum\nbash install.sh" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

## Useful options

Use the default choices without prompts:

{% set command_id = "install-yes" %}{% set command_label = "No prompts" %}{% set command_text = "bash install.sh --yes" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

Review or resume an installation:

{% set command_id = "install-options" %}{% set command_label = "Review / Resume" %}{% set command_text = "pegasus install --review\npegasus install --resume" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

## After installation

Open the Pegasus Control Center:

{% set command_id = "control-center" %}{% set command_label = "Control Center" %}{% set command_text = "pegasus" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

You can also find **Pegasus Control Center** in GNOME Applications.

### Themes

{% set command_id = "theme-commands" %}{% set command_label = "Themes" %}{% set command_text = "pegasus theme\npegasus theme list\npegasus theme apply Nord" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

### Check your setup

{% set command_id = "doctor" %}{% set command_label = "Diagnostics" %}{% set command_text = "pegasus doctor" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

### Update or uninstall

{% set command_id = "maintenance" %}{% set command_label = "Maintenance" %}{% set command_text = "pegasus update\npegasus uninstall" %}{% include "components/command-block.njk" %}

## Optional integrations

ASDControl, Google Chrome, Alacritty, Flameshot, and Ulauncher are optional. Pegasus configures them only when they are already installed.

Pegasus is built for Fedora Workstation and inspired by [Omakub](https://omakub.org).
